### 8. Error Handling Rules

#### Async Operations

```typescript
// Frontend error handling
async function handleAsyncOperation() {
  try {
    const result = await window.electronAPI.someOperation();
    if (result.success) {
      // Handle success
    } else {
      addDebugLog(`Operation failed: ${result.error}`);
    }
  } catch (error) {
    addDebugLog(`Unexpected error: ${error}`);
  }
}
```

#### Main Process Error Handling

```javascript
// Graceful error handling in main process
ipcMain.handle("operation", async (event, params) => {
  try {
    const result = await performOperation(params);
    return { success: true, data: result };
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Operation failed:", error);
    return { success: false, error: error.message };
  }
});
```

### 9. Browser Integration Rules

#### URL Navigation

```typescript
// Handle different URL types
async function navigateToUrl(url: string) {
  // Ensure proper protocol
  if (!url.startsWith("http://") && !url.startsWith("https://")) {
    url = "https://" + url;
  }

  // Navigate via Electron BrowserView
  const result = await window.electronAPI.navigateUrl(url);
  if (result.success) {
    setIsWebView(true);
    await window.electronAPI.showBrowser();
  }
}
```

#### Browser Controls

```typescript
// Navigation controls
const controls = {
  back: () => window.electronAPI.browserBack(),
  forward: () => window.electronAPI.browserForward(),
  reload: () => window.electronAPI.browserReload(),
  stop: () => window.electronAPI.browserStop(),
};
```

### 10. LLM Autofill Development Rules (v2.0.0)

#### Backend-Only Implementation

- **NO UI CHANGES**: Maintain existing visual design, layout, and styling
- **Cursor States Only**: Implement cursor state management for user feedback
- **Focus Management**: Place caret at end of inserted text, no auto-advance
- **Error Handling**: Graceful fallback to existing autofill system

#### Performance Requirements

```javascript
// Performance targets
const PERFORMANCE_TARGETS = {
  P95_LATENCY: 3000, // 3 seconds max
  MIN_RAM_GB: 8, // Minimum hardware
  IDLE_TIMEOUT: 30, // Minutes before unload
  MAX_MEMORY_GB: 4, // Model memory limit
};

// Hardware detection
async function checkHardwareRequirements() {
  const ram = await getSystemRAM();
  if (ram < PERFORMANCE_TARGETS.MIN_RAM_GB) {
    throw new Error(
      `Insufficient RAM: ${ram}GB < ${PERFORMANCE_TARGETS.MIN_RAM_GB}GB`
    );
  }
}
```

